    "eco-toxicology",
    "regulatory toxicology"
   ],
   "dateReleased": "1986",
   "dateSource": "https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/base-de-donnees-agritox",
   "creator": "INRA; ANSES",
   "url": "https://www.data.gouv.fr/fr/datasets/base-de-donnees-agritox/",
   "description": "French database of pesticide active substances, created by INRA and now run by ANSES. It holds expert-validated data from regulatory dossiers and the literature: identity, physicochemical properties, acute toxicity, reference values (ADI, ARfD, AOEL), ecotoxicity and classification. The data are released as open files, so regulatory pesticide hazard data can be reused.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "absent",
   "mentionedIn": [
    "FAIRSharing"
   ],
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.73888a",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. The producer page (ANSES on data.gouv.fr) says INRA created AGRITOX in 1986, matching the FAIRsharing year. That is a creation year; online availability is documented only from the first web capture on inra.fr/agritox (2001-07-22). Linked from eChemPortal since 2011-03-09. agritox.anses.fr no longer resolves; data are now published as open files on data.gouv.fr (last update 2026-06-10). Stakeholder Regulator: the data were validated by official assessment bodies and ANSES maintains it, although INRA is a research institute. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A database that indexes and serves records under stable identifiers, typed Domain-specific registry as databases are in FIPs.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
   "qualifiedAttribution": [
    {
     "@type": "prov:Attribution",
     "hadRole": "Regulator"
    }
   ]
  },
