   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): The AOP-KB was established by the OECD with the EU reference laboratory (JRC) and US EPA in 2014 (Environ Health Toxicol 2018, doi:10.5620/eht.e2018002; Martens et al. 2018, doi:10.3389/fgene.2018.00661: 'emerged in 2014'). Its first module, AOP-Wiki 1.0, was released 2014-09-28, and the aopkb.org hub page was captured 2014-12-01. aopkb.oecd.org served an AOP/KE search hub until June 2026 and has redirected (301) to aopwiki.org/aops since August 2026. I marked it active because the content lives on in the AOP-Wiki; 'discontinued' is also defensible for the hub page itself. I found no FAIRsharing DOI record through DataCite. Verified 5 Oct 2026: maintained changed (https://aopkb.oecd.org now answers HTTP 301 to https://aopwiki.org/aops (checked 2026-10-05). The AOP-KB hub and its search no longer exist as a resource of their own; only the AOP-Wiki, which has its own row, continues. 'active' (maintained and available) does not fit a homepage that permanently redirects to another resource.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Declared in a FIP as the F4 registry indexing AOPs, it supports AOP development and their OECD review for regulatory use.",
