   "url": "https://cebs.niehs.nih.gov/cebs/",
   "description": "Public NIEHS repository of toxicology study data: the individual-animal and summary data of the US National Toxicology Program studies, and data deposited by academic, industrial and government laboratories, held with their study design so that studies can be compared and combined. It holds the NTP data collections (now DTT Data Collections) and the complete DrugMatrix database.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "absent",
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.ntv8pe",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "reviewedBy": "GC",
   "note": "Co-author addition 30 Oct 2026 (GC, overview of toxicogenomics data, analysis and integration). Research 30 Oct 2026 (high confidence): first description Waters et al., EHP Toxicogenomics 111(1T), January 2003 (PubMed 12735106); the DOI 10.1289/ehp.5971 carries its EHP version of May 2003. FAIRsharing year 2003. Lea et al., NAR 2017 (doi 10.1093/nar/gkw1077): CEBS compiles the individual and summary animal data of the NTP testing programme and of other depositors. CEBS is cited as https://doi.org/10.22427/NTP-DATA-1; its NTP Data Collections were renamed DTT Data Collections in September 2025 (release v7.5.2), and release v7.6.1 came out on 24 June 2026. The National Toxicology Program itself would be E1, so CEBS stands for its data.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
   "qualifiedAttribution": [
