   "dateSource": "http://web.archive.org/web/20190821200437/https://gsbl.de/",
   "creator": "German federal and Länder authorities (ChemInfo cooperation, UBA)",
   "url": "https://recherche.chemikalieninfo.de/",
   "description": "Chemical information system run jointly by the German federal and state authorities as the successor of the GSBL substance data pool. For each substance it compiles identity, physicochemical, toxicological and ecotoxicological data, environmental occurrence, hazard and emergency-response information and the relevant legal provisions. A public subset can be searched without registration; the full data set is open to authorities and emergency services.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "absent",
   "mentionedIn": [
    "FAIRSharing"
   ],
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.b5a070",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): The history section on chemikalieninfo.de says the GSBL agreement ended on 2015-12-31, the ChemInfo cooperation started on 2016-01-01 and the online search application was completed in December 2021. Web-archive captures of recherche.chemikalieninfo.de start in 2022-01. The predecessor 'GSBL public' was online by 2003 (gsbl.de capture); use 2003 instead if the GSBL lineage should count. There is no FAIRsharing year. Scope, stakeholder and subdomains filled (were empty). Include: member of the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection (I4). Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (ChemInfo could be searched publicly under its own name before the December 2021 relaunch. The gsbl.de homepage captured 2019-08-21 reads 'Willkommen bei ChemInfo! ... Unsere Datenbank ist weiterhin uneingeschänkt für Sie verfügbar ... Stoffinformationssystem ChemInfo public, einem Auszug aus dem Gesamtsystem', with a link to the public search (http://web.archive.org/web/20190821200437/https://gsbl.de/). The 2019-04-04 capture still says 'GSBL public', so 2019 is a lower bound. December 2021 is only when the rebuilt search application was completed (chemikalieninfo.de history). Use 2003 instead if the GSBL lineage counts, as the note says.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (Source for the 2019 lower bound (see datePublished). dateBasis stays release.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A database that indexes and serves records under stable identifiers, typed Domain-specific registry as databases are in FIPs.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
