   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.bca16f",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): FAIRsharing year 2004 kept. The database's own terms of use (archived DTU page, http://web.archive.org/web/20121021213223/http://qsar.food.dtu.dk/) describe it as a public snapshot of the Danish EPA (Q)SAR tool as of 1 Jan 2004, made with support from the European Chemicals Bureau. The exact first release date was not found; the DTU host is captured from 2012-10. Stakeholder set to In silico research (QSAR modellers, now at DTU); because the first version came from the Danish EPA, Regulator is the alternative. Include: member of the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection (I4). Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (2004 is not a release date. It is when the Danish EPA-ECB project to build an internet version began ('In 2004, a collaborative project was set up between the Danish EPA and the ECB to develop an internet-accessible version', http://web.archive.org/web/20060507054905/http://ecb.jrc.it/QSAR/qsar_tools/), and it is the date of the data snapshot. The ECB 'What's new' for April 2006 announces the registration form for the internet version of the Danish (Q)SAR database (http://web.archive.org/web/20070502164010/http://ecb.jrc.it:80/whatsnew/content1.php?ANNEE=2006). The ECB news for 2004-2005 does not mention it. The method uses the FAIRsharing year only as a last resort.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateBasis changed (An agency page documents the public release (see datePublished), so the FAIRsharing-year fallback no longer applies.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (ECB 'What's new' 2006, April entry announcing access to the internet version of the Danish (Q)SAR database.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A database that indexes and serves records under stable identifiers, typed Domain-specific registry as databases are in FIPs.",
