   "description": "DataCure is an OpenRiskNet case study that built API-based workflows and Jupyter/Squonk notebooks. These retrieve, curate, semantically annotate and merge toxicology datasets (e.g. ToxCast/Tox21, Open TG-GATEs, ChEMBL, LTKB) so they can be reused for modelling and read-across.",
   "maintained": "discontinued",
   "manuscript": "cited",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Computational; L149",
   "fairsharingMatch": "no record",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (low confidence): The row had no date. DataCure is defined in OpenRiskNet deliverable D1.3 'Final definition of case studies'. The document was finalised 2017-12-18 and became public on Zenodo 2018-11-07. Later dates: notebooks in github.com/OpenRiskNet/notebooks/DataCure from 2019-02-08, D4.2 (final 2019-02-21), webinar 2019-03-18, case-study page first archived 2019-08-22, case-study report 2019-12-11. Use 2019-02-08 if only released artefacts should count. OpenRiskNet ended in November 2019 and its services are offline. Doubt on I1: DataCure is a project case study; the reusable outputs are the curation workflows and notebooks. FAIRsharing: no record. Verified 5 Oct 2026: decision changed (DataCure is a project case study, so it fails I1. Its own page is titled 'Case Study DataCure' (https://openrisknet.org/e-infrastructure/development/case-studies/case-study-datacure/), and OpenRiskNet D1.3 defines it as one of the project's case studies (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1479127). Its reusable outputs are notebooks in the OpenRiskNet repository, which belong to the openrisknet e-infrastructure row. The sibling case study AOPLink, named in the same manuscript sentence (L149), is already excluded with E1. The row's own note already doubts I1.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: exclusionReason changed (The decision changes to exclude. DataCure is an initiative within the OpenRiskNet project (a case study), the same code as the AOPLink row (https://openrisknet.org/e-infrastructure/development/case-studies/case-study-datacure/).)",
