   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (low confidence): The row had no date; 2018 is a lower bound only. The OpenRiskNet poster (issued 2018-03-12) already describes searching ToxCast and TG-GATEs through 'the data explorer'. D1.3 (final 2017-12-18) lists 'Data Explorer (DC)', and the ToxCast API code on GitHub (douglasconnect/opentox-toxcast) dates from November 2016, so 2017 is possible. The site was first archived 2019-07-21. The site and its ToxCast, ToxRefDB and Open TG-GATEs APIs still respond (Oct 2026) but serve old data releases (e.g. ToxCast October 2015), so maintenance status is unknown. Added 'toxicogenomics' for Open TG-GATEs. FAIRsharing: no record. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (Thomas Exner's talk at OpenTox USA 2017 (Durham, 12 July 2017) is on Zenodo with publication date 2017-07-12 (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.831444). Slides 13-14 are screenshots of the running 'DC Data Explorer - Collection of toxicological data sources exposed via OpenTox', with ToxRefDB, ToxCast/Tox21 and Open TG-Gates tabs. This is 8 months before the March 2018 poster. The basis stays 'release' as a lower bound.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (The earlier public evidence is the July 2017 OpenTox USA slides, which show the DC Data Explorer by name (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.831444).) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A REST API and web interface giving harmonised access across ToxCast/Tox21, ToxRefDB and TG-GATEs data, used to integrate them into workflows.",
