   "reviewedBy": "IM",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): Refined 2015 (print issue, May 2015) to the online date 2014-12-12 (Crossref, Europe PMC). The portal named in the paper, www.dixa-fp7.eu, is now a parked domain and the EBI warehouse URL redirects to a team page, so the URL stays the DOI and discontinued is confirmed. FAIRsharing: no DOI-bearing record found via DataCite; records without a DOI not checked. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (On 2013-08-27 the diXa homepage linked the Data Warehouse only in its 'Members' box (https://web.archive.org/web/20130827153007/http://www.dixa-fp7.eu/). By 2014-02-07 the homepage had a public 'Enter the diXa data warehouse' button linking to wwwdev.ebi.ac.uk/fg/dixa (https://web.archive.org/web/20140207104020/http://www.dixa-fp7.eu/). So the warehouse was public about 10 months before the paper's online date. A capture is only a lower bound, so year precision is used, as for SEND. The workshop report describing diXa (doi 10.1007/s00204-014-1387-3, online 2014-10-19) also comes before the paper.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateBasis changed (The earliest documented date is the public availability (launch) of the warehouse, shown in a web archive capture, not the 2014-12-12 paper.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (This is the earliest capture showing the public 'Enter the diXa data warehouse' entry point. The Aug 2013 capture still lists the warehouse under Members only.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Domain repository for toxicogenomics data that took deposits through templates and linked chemical, molecular and phenotype records, acting on deposition and integration. IM: Instead ChemAgora can be used here)https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset/jrc-eurl-ecvam-chemagora",
