   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.4b2234",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): The archived 1999 ECOTOX FAQ says the combined ECOTOX interface was released to government users only, by telnet, in March 1996, and that AQUIRE was opened to all users on the web in 1999. The public ECOTOX homepage was captured on 1999-08-27 (page last modified 1999-05-04). FAIRsharing year 2017 is far too late. Olker et al. 2022 (https://doi.org/10.1002/etc.5324) describes version 5, not the launch. ECOTOX data tapes were also sold through NTIS, date not established. Include: member of the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection (I4). Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (NTIS sold ECOTOX itself to the public in 1996. Record PB97500318, 'Ecotox Database (AQUIRE, PHYTOTOX, and TERRETOX) (VMS Data and Programs) (on Magnetic Tape)', has publication date 1996 and NTIS issue 1997-01, and supersedes the 1995 AQUIRE tapes (https://ntrl.ntis.gov/NTRL/dashboard/searchResults/titleDetail/PB97500318.xhtml). The non-VMS tape, PB97500292, is also dated 1996. The cited 1999 FAQ lists both tapes. 1999 is only when AQUIRE opened on the web.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (Source for the 1996 NTIS release (see datePublished). dateBasis stays release.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A database that indexes and serves records under stable identifiers, typed Domain-specific registry as databases are in FIPs.",
