   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): The row had no date. EFSA Journal 23(11), November 2025; the DOI was registered 2025-11-13 (Crossref, OpenAlex). The panel adoption date was not checked because the Wiley and EFSA pages refuse automated requests; use it with dateBasis 'adoption' if preferred. The statement was prepared by EFSA's working group on effect models in environmental risk assessment. Added 'eco-toxicology' and 'computational and predictive toxicology', since it concerns mechanistic effect models for environmental risk assessment of pesticides. The creator was 'EFSA (EFSA Journal 2025)' and is now 'EFSA'. FAIRsharing: no record. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (EFSA's own page for the statement, archived on 13 Nov 2025, reads 'Published: 13 November 2025, Adopted: 29 October 2025' (https://web.archive.org/web/20251113112641/https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/9741). Under the rules, official adoption of guidance is an allowed earliest date, and it comes before the 2025-11-13 Crossref deposit.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateBasis changed (The row is the guidance itself (Policy: institution), and the corrected date is EFSA's adoption date of 29 Oct 2025 (https://web.archive.org/web/20251113112641/https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/9741). The data dictionary defines 'adoption' as the official adoption or publication of guidance.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (Crossref and the Wiley DOI landing page show only the deposit and issue dates, and Wiley refuses scripted requests. The archived EFSA page shows the adoption date (29 Oct 2025).) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: EFSA's authoritative interpretation of the FAIR principles for mechanistic effect models, applying from the underlying data through model code to regulatory model assessment.",
