   ],
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.r18yt0",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "reviewedBy": "IM",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): Kept the paper's online date, 2015-07-27 (Crossref, Europe PMC). data.enanomapper.net was already online by 2015-01-29 (earliest Wayback capture), and FAIRsharing gives 2014, so the launch may be earlier; no public evidence from before 2015 was found. REST API live on 2026-10-05; the root URL returns HTTP 405, and the search UI is at search.data.enanomapper.net (redirects to enanomapper.adma.ai). Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (The 2015 Beilstein paper itself says 'We have recently described the design of the eNanoMapper prototype database [10]' (Europe PMC PMC4578352). Ref. 10 is Jeliazkova et al., 'The first eNanoMapper prototype: A substance database to support safe-by-design', IEEE BIBM 2014, held in Belfast on 2-5 Nov 2014; Crossref gives issued 2014-11 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1109/BIBM.2014.6999367). That paper is the first description of the database, and it matches FAIRsharing's year of 2014. The basis stays publication.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (Points to the first describing paper, the BIBM 2014 proceedings paper on the eNanoMapper prototype database (Crossref issued 2014-11), which the 2015 paper cites as its earlier description.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A nanosafety repository that receives data through templates and serves harmonised, searchable records for reuse, acting at deposit and in data integration.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
