   ],
   "reviewedBy": "IM",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): Date: Pognan et al., Pharmaceuticals, online 2021-03-08 (Crossref), the first full description of the ToxHub; confirms the previous inventory's 2021. E4 proposed because the hub was never public. The paper says ToxHub ran in a secure cloud for eTRANSAFE partners. The project's 'Publicly accessible results' page (http://web.archive.org/web/20230608060414/https://etransafe.eu/publicly-accessible-results/) lists Flame, Rosetta Stone, PretoxTM, models and code, but not the hub. The etransafe.eu domain has lapsed, so the URL is the paper DOI. Co-authors to confirm, as docs/inclusion-criteria.md asks for this row. FAIRsharing not searched because the web-search budget had run out. Verified 5 Oct 2026: decision changed (docs/inclusion-criteria.md §5 'Availability' names the eTRANSAFE knowledge hub as a row that stays undecided until the co-authors confirm I3, and this row's note says the co-authors still have to confirm. The evidence supports E4 only as a proposal. Pognan et al. 2021 (PMC7999019, https://doi.org/10.3390/ph14030237) says ToxHub ran in a secure cloud with components open to eTRANSAFE partners. The archived 'Publicly accessible results' page (http://web.archive.org/web/20230608060414/https://etransafe.eu/publicly-accessible-results/) does not list the hub.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: exclusionReason changed (Cleared because the decision returns to undecided. E4 stays as the proposal in the note.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A database that indexes and serves records under stable identifiers, typed Domain-specific registry as databases are in FIPs.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
