   "datePublished": "2020-07-06",
   "dateSource": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00204-020-02802-6",
   "creator": "EU-ToxRisk consortium (Edelweiss Connect)",
   "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tiv.2024.105903",
   "description": "The data and knowledge management infrastructure of the EU-ToxRisk project. It combines a common data and metadata format, a methods database documenting test protocols, data archiving, an API for access to individual data points, analysis notebooks and a knowledge portal. It was built to make in vitro new approach method data from many laboratories documented, shareable and reusable for risk assessment.",
   "maintained": "unknown",
   "manuscript": "cited",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Data generation; Comments [r]; L101, L103, L373",
   "mentionedIn": [
    "Whitepaper"
   ],
   "reviewedBy": "IM",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): Refined to 2020-07-06, the online date of Krebs et al. 2020. That paper reports the EU-ToxRisk method documentation pipeline and a public test-method database (eu-toxrisk.douglasconnect.com/public). The full infrastructure is described in Hardy et al. 2024 (e-pub 2024-07-22; Edelweiss Connect). Maintained changed from active to unknown: on 2026-10-05 that database returned HTTP 400 and eu-toxrisk.eu showed a hosting error, although Hardy 2024 says the system is being extended for RISK-HUNT3R/ASPIS. Stakeholder kept, but In silico research would also fit because a data-management firm built it. FAIRsharing: no DOI-bearing record found via DataCite; records without a DOI not checked. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Archives in vitro data and protocols in a common format as labs record them, and integrates results across laboratories through an API and portal.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
   "qualifiedAttribution": [
