     "hadRole": "related_to",
     "evidence": "literature",
     "source": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00204-020-02802-6",
     "note": "Checked 5 Oct 2026: Krebs et al. 2020 report that EU-ToxRisk used BioStudies as the data warehouse of its knowledge platform, and BioStudies still hosts an EU-ToxRisk collection (about 1,300 S-TOXR studies); a repository is not a standard, so related_to is the right label."
    }
   ]
