   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): The GEO news page (archived August 2000) dates the relaunch of the GEO website, with the repository open for submissions and all submissions publicly accessible, to 2000-07-25. An informational site without the repository went up in October 1999. Clough & Barrett 2016 (doi 10.1007/978-1-4939-3578-9_5) say NCBI launched the GEO database in 2000, and sample GSM1 has been public since 2000-09-28. First paper: Edgar et al., NAR 2002 (doi 10.1093/nar/30.1.207). The FAIRsharing record FAIRsharing.5hc8vt is Database/repository with year 2002. Verified 5 Oct 2026: fairsharingMatch changed (One lookup of https://fairsharing.org/FAIRsharing.5hc8vt returns id 1975 'Gene Expression Omnibus' (GEO): Database/repository, homepage https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/. This is identical to the row's name and URL.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Declared for F4 and F1: GEO indexes functional genomics records for search and assigns them stable accessions, so registry and identifier service.",
