   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (low confidence): Earliest evidence found, used as a lower bound: Purchase 1989 (Pol J Occup Med 2(4):337-49, PMID 2489435) reports that IPCS produces ICSCs. Later evidence: a 1992 review of the printed cards (https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-3894(92)87024-a), 349 English cards by 1993 (PMID 8255257), online at NIOSH by 1997-1998 (web archive) and in the ILO database later. The project start date was not found and there is no FAIRsharing year. URL updated to the page the old one now redirects to. Include: member of the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection (I4). Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateBasis changed (Purchase 1989 (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2489435/) reviews international work on existing chemicals and only mentions that IPCS produces ICSCs. It is not the paper that first describes the cards, so 1989 is a lower bound for their release. This fits WHO's World Health of December 1988, which announced 'the planned publication of some 400 ... International Chemical Safety Cards this year and next' (https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/52739).) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A database that indexes and serves records under stable identifiers, typed Domain-specific registry as databases are in FIPs.",
