   "creator": "EMBL-EBI",
   "url": "https://identifiers.org",
   "description": "Identifiers.org is an EMBL-EBI registry and resolver that gives life-science data collections a namespace prefix and resolves compact identifiers (prefix:accession) and identifiers.org URIs to the matching data record. It makes references to data stable, globally unique and resolvable, which supports the annotation of models and datasets.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "named",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Computational; L147",
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.2b0d92",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): The first description is Juty, Le Novère & Laibe, NAR Database issue, published online 2011-12-02 (Crossref/Europe PMC). The earliest web capture of identifiers.org is 2012-07-25. The service grew out of the MIRIAM Registry (2006), which FAIRsharing lists as 'Identifiers.org Central Registry' (FAIRsharing.n14rc8, database, year 2006). The record that fits this identifier-schema row is 'Identifiers.org namespace' (FAIRsharing.2b0d92, Standard/identifier_schema, year 2012). I found it through DataCite (prefix 10.25504) and confirmed it with one JSON lookup. Homepage responded on 2026-10-05. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (The Identifiers.org news page (captured 2012-07-27: https://web.archive.org/web/20120727025443/http://identifiers.org/news) lists for 2011: 'July: Beta version of Identifiers.org goes live' and 'September: Identifiers.org leaves the beta stage!'. The NAR paper (received 2011-09-16) also calls the URL scheme 'recently introduced'. The service was therefore public months before the 2011-12-02 paper. Use 2011-09 if a public beta should not count.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateBasis changed (The earliest event is the public (beta) launch in July 2011, not the paper.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (This news page dates the launch: July 2011, beta live.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: fairsharingMatch changed (One JSON lookup of https://fairsharing.org/FAIRsharing.2b0d92 returns 'Identifiers.org namespace', Standard/identifier_schema, status ready, homepage docs.identifiers.org/pages/identification_scheme.html. Its description is the Identifiers.org compact-identifier resolution service, which matches this identifier-schema row.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Registry and resolver of namespace prefixes and compact identifiers that makes data references globally unique and resolvable, an identifier service.",
