   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (low confidence): Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. FAIRsharing gives no year, and no official launch date was found. The JRC's IPCheM portal was online by 2014-11-26 (earliest archive capture; a lower bound, showing modules and participation information). By Dec 2015 'IPCheM Version 3.1' offered data discovery and a viewer (archive). Modules are coordinated by EEA, EFSA and JRC. URL trailing '#' dropped. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (The 2014-11-26 capture (https://web.archive.org/web/20141126151332/http://ipchem.jrc.ec.europa.eu/) is only a public information page: a June 2014 flyer, 'How to participate' and LIFE funding. Its only links into the platform are 'Go to IPCheM for European Agencies' (webgate.ec.testa.eu, the closed sTESTA network) and 'Go to IPCheM for European Commission' (ipchem-portal.jrc.it, internal to JRC). The platform was therefore not publicly available in 2014. The first capture of the public discovery portal (IPCheM Version 3.1, with Discovery and Viewer) is from 2015-12-19, so 2015 is the documented lower bound.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (Earliest capture of the publicly accessible IPCheM portal (Version 3.1); see datePublished.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A portal that receives and indexes chemical monitoring data collections, harmonises them and offers one access point for exposure and risk assessment.",
