   "url": "https://isa-tools.org",
   "description": "The ISA framework is a general Investigation-Study-Assay metadata model, with ISA-Tab as its tab-delimited format and a set of supporting tools, for describing multi-omics and other life-science experiments. It records study design, sample characteristics, protocols and data files, so experimental metadata can be reported consistently, validated and reused.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "cited",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Data generation; Comments [ap]; L99-100, L407",
   "mentionedIn": [
    "INTOXICOM 1"
   ],
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.53gp75",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): The year is confirmed. The first description is the RSBI ISA-TAB workshop report, OMICS 12(2) (Crossref issue/online date 2008-06-01; PubMed 2008 Jun). The DOI was registered on 2008-04-30 and PubMed indexed it on 2008-05-02, so the online date is uncertain and I kept year precision. The format was proposed at the workshop held 6-8 Dec 2007 at the EBI, where toxicogenomics was among the RSBI communities. FAIRsharing yearCreation 2010 reflects the ISA software suite. I refined the creator because ISA-Tab started at EMBL-EBI before the team moved to Oxford. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A FIP declares it for F2; ISA is a metadata model and tabular format for describing study design, samples, protocols and data files.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
