   "url": "https://elixir-europe.github.io/MARS/",
   "description": "MARS (Multi-omics Adapter for Repository Submissions) is an ELIXIR framework, with a command-line tool and repository adapters, for submitting a multi-omics study described in ISA-JSON to several public repositories (BioSamples, ENA, MetaboLights) in one go. It aims to keep metadata and accession numbers consistent across those repositories.",
   "maintained": "in development",
   "manuscript": "named",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Data generation; Comments [m]; L99, L363",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): There is no release, tag or paper. The GitHub history starts with an initial commit on 2023-05-26, with public work at BioHackathon Europe 2023 (commits 2023-10-30/11-01). The MARS site traces the project back to BioHackathon Europe 2022, and a BioHackathon 2024 report draft is in paper.md. The earliest web capture is 2024-05-11. The status page shows proofs of concept, none deployed, hence 'in development'. I changed the URL to the project website (the repo is github.com/elixir-europe/MARS). I removed 'computational and predictive toxicology' because MARS is a submission tool, not a model. I found no FAIRsharing DOI record through DataCite; FAIRsharing does not register software. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Framework that automates submitting ISA-JSON-described multi-omics studies to several public repositories, publishing them with consistent metadata and accessions.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Supporting-Resource",
   "qualifiedRelation": [
    {
     "relation": "https://doi.org/10.25504/FAIRsharing.yhLgTV",
     "hadRole": "implements",
     "evidence": "literature",
     "source": "https://elixir-europe.github.io/MARS/#isa-json-as-metadata-carrier",
     "note": "The MARS site: ISA-JSON is the metadata carrier of MARS, used to store and exchange metadata between end users and the target repositories, with a MARS ISA-JSON schema of its own. Proposed by JH on 29 Oct 2026."
    }
   ]
  },
