   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.32b10v",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): Brazma et al., Nat Genet 29(4), December 2001 issue (Crossref issued 2001-12; PubMed 2001 Dec; FGED history: 'December 2001 - a paper describing MIAME was published'). Draft MGED standard proposals were posted from December 1999, which matches FAIRsharing year 1999 (MGED founding). Discontinued is confirmed: fged.org says the FGED Society closed operations in 2021. MIAME is still used by repositories. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (The MGED annotations working-group page (captured 2001-02-20, page 'Last modified: Friday, December 15, 2000': https://web.archive.org/web/20010220163059/http://www.mged.org/Annotations-wg/index.html) publishes the full 'Minimum information about a microarray experiment - MIAME', marked 'Endorsed by MGED steering committee meeting November 17, 2000'. The Nat Genet paper's acknowledgements confirm that the Nov 2000 NIH steering-committee meeting prepared the current version. MIAME was officially adopted and public a year before the Dec 2001 paper. If release is preferred over adoption, use 2000 with basis release.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateBasis changed (This is the formal endorsement of the guideline by MGED, comparable to the W3C Recommendation dates used with 'adoption' for rdf/owl/sparql.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (This capture shows the MIAME text with its 17 Nov 2000 endorsement and a 15 Dec 2000 last-modified date.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Minimum-information reporting guideline listing the metadata needed to interpret and reproduce microarray experiments, hence a metadata schema.",
