   "creator": "NORMAN Association",
   "url": "https://www.norman-network.com/nds/susdat/",
   "description": "Merged and curated database of more than 100,000 substances of environmental concern, compiled from the suspect lists contributed to the NORMAN Suspect List Exchange. It adds harmonised identifiers (CAS, SMILES, InChIKey, PubChem CID, DTXSID), MS-ready structures and predicted properties and ecotoxicity thresholds. It supports suspect and non-target screening, prioritisation and exposure assessment of emerging contaminants.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "absent",
   "mentionedIn": [
    "Whitepaper",
    "FAIRSharing"
   ],
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.9ATgeT",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. FAIRsharing year 2015 confirmed as the start of the NORMAN Suspect List Exchange (NORMAN-SLE), which FAIRsharing counts as part of this resource (Mohammed Taha et al. 2022, doi 10.1186/s12302-022-00680-6). The merged SusDat table was online by 2017-06-25 (archive of norman-network.com/datatable). Dulio et al. 2018 (doi 10.1186/s12302-018-0135-3) call it recently launched. The first Zenodo version was issued 2018-03-01 (doi 10.5281/zenodo.2664078). Use 2017 if SusDat alone is meant. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (The cited paper (Mohammed Taha et al. 2022, https://doi.org/10.1186/s12302-022-00680-6) dates only the start of the NORMAN Suspect List Exchange to 2015. It also says SusDat 'will be described in more detail in a separate article'. The row, its url and its FAIRsharing homepage are SusDat. 'NORMAN-SusDat: NORMAN Suspect List Exchange Merged Data Table' was first captured on 2017-06-25. Dulio et al. 2018 (received 2017-10-25, https://doi.org/10.1186/s12302-018-0135-3) says SusDat 'has recently been launched', citing that datatable. The Zenodo S0 SUSDAT record was created on 2019-05-04 (with a backdated publication date of 2018-03-01). The basis stays release.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (Earliest documented public availability of the merged SusDat table (a lower bound); see datePublished.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: A database that indexes and serves records under stable identifiers, typed Domain-specific registry as databases are in FIPs.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
