   "url": "https://obi-ontology.org",
   "description": "The Ontology for Biomedical Investigations (OBI) is an OBO Foundry ontology of terms for describing biomedical investigations: study designs, protocols, instruments, materials, assays and data transformations. It supports consistent, machine-readable annotation of experimental metadata.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "named",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Data generation (nano); L109",
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.284e1z",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): I corrected the date from 2009. 2009 matches the OBI release of 2009-11-02 used in Brinkman et al. 2010 (doi:10.1186/2041-1480-1-S1-S7), but an OBI OWL file was already public at obi.sourceforge.net (web capture 2007-08-07). The OBI site, which says OBI was renamed from FuGO, existed by Jan 2007, and the SourceForge project was created 2006-09-20. FuGO, the predecessor, was described in OMICS 2006 (doi:10.1089/omi.2006.10.199). FAIRsharing gives 2008, and the main paper is Bandrowski et al., PLoS One 2016 (the previous source). 2007 is used as a web-archive lower bound. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (OBI is FuGO renamed: 'The FuGO effort was rechristened the Ontology for Biomedical Investigations' (Bandrowski et al. 2016, PMC4851331). FuGO was first described in OMICS 10(2) 2006 (doi:10.1089/omi.2006.10.199; Crossref print 2006-06, online 2006-07). FuGO.owl itself (223 classes) was public at fugo.sourceforge.net/ontology/FuGO.owl by 2006-09-06 (https://web.archive.org/web/20060906041903/http://fugo.sourceforge.net/ontology/FuGO.owl). Both are earlier than the 2007 OBI.owl capture.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateBasis changed (The earliest event is the 2006 OMICS paper that first describes the ontology (as FuGO). FuGO.owl was also public in 2006.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (Whetzel et al., 'Development of FuGO: an ontology for functional genomics investigations', OMICS 2006, is the first describing paper of OBI under its original name.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: OBO ontology giving controlled terms and relations that model investigations, protocols, assays and data transformations for machine-readable experimental metadata.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource"
  },
