   "url": "https://co.mbine.org/standards/omex",
   "description": "OMEX (the COMBINE archive format) is a ZIP-based container with a manifest that packs all files of a modelling project (models, simulation descriptions, data and metadata) into one exchangeable file. It lets computational models and their simulation experiments be shared and reproduced as a single package.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "cited",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Computational; L146, L150",
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.27tnee",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): The COMBINE specification record says 'Version 1 of the OMEX specification was published on September 15, 2014'. This is earlier than the previously used BMC Bioinformatics paper (online 2014-12-14, doi:10.1186/s12859-014-0369-z). FAIRsharing year 2014 agrees. I changed maintained from unknown to active: OMEX is still a current COMBINE standard (the OMEX metadata specs 1.0/1.2 build on it). co.mbine.org/standards/omex now redirects through identifiers.org to the COMBINE specifications record. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Container format whose manifest and metadata describe each file of a modelling project and link that metadata to the packaged files.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
