   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): The year 2018 is confirmed and now has a full date. The first public description of the e-infrastructure is the OpenRiskNet poster on Zenodo (issued 2018-03-12). D3.2 'First documentation of the core e-infrastructure' was finalised 2017-12-06 but only made public on Zenodo 2018-11-12. The project ran from December 2016 to November 2019. The website (first archived 2017-06-23) is still online, but the reference environment (home.prod.openrisknet.org) is offline. FAIRsharing: no record. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (The same OpenTox USA talk of 12 July 2017 (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.831444) describes the e-infrastructure before the poster does. It runs under the header 'OpenRiskNet: Open e-Infrastructure to Support Data Sharing...', has a slide 'OpenRiskNet - Risk Assessment E-Infrastructure' describing it, and demonstrates its first harmonised data APIs (ToxCast, ToxRefDB, TG-GATEs), the data explorer and KNIME integration. The note's claim that the 2018-03-12 poster is the first public description therefore does not hold.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (The earliest public description of the OpenRiskNet e-infrastructure is the July 2017 OpenTox USA presentation on Zenodo (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.831444).) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: E-infrastructure connecting semantically annotated data and modelling services through APIs and making them discoverable, used to integrate data into predictive models.",
