   "creator": "PARC (Chemicals Toxicology Community)",
   "url": "https://w3id.org/np/RAKa7vUwc8qVbktDqDSpuq7lRrrKcjPKvkB4Tn7WHvr7E",
   "description": "This is the FAIR Implementation Profile of the PARC Chemicals Toxicology Community. It declares which FAIR-enabling resources the community uses for each FAIR principle and is published as machine-readable nanopublications from the FIP Wizard.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "named",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Table 1; Comments [g]; L60",
   "fairsharingMatch": "no record",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): The year 2026 is confirmed and now has a full date. The 'PARC Toxicology' FIP v0.1.0 nanopublication has dct:created 2026-09-07. It comes from FIP Wizard project 618ed60e, drafted since September 2023, with creators from the University of Birmingham and GO FAIR Foundation. The same PARC Toxicology community published earlier FIPs: 'PARC TOXRIC FIP' (first nanopublication 2023-04-17, updated 2024-01-22) and 'PARC Toxicology rFIP' v0.0.1 (2025-06-25) and v0.0.2 (2026-03-02). If the row stands for PARC toxicology FIPs in general, use 2023-04-17. Type changed from 'Standard: model/format' to 'Collection' to match fairaop, since a FIP lists the FAIR-enabling resources a community chose. FAIRsharing: no record. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: The PARC Chemicals Toxicology community's FIP, declaring for each FAIR principle the FAIR-enabling resources it uses, published as nanopublications. Checked 30 Oct 2026 (MM): declared by the PARC Toxicology community (row parctoxicology), whose description includes the development of adverse outcome pathways, yet none of the 89 declarations of v0.1.0 names an AOP resource (AOP-Wiki, AOP-KB, AOP Ontology); AOP resources are declared only in the Reference AOP FIP (fairaop). Listed in the PARC space https://w3id.org/spaces/parc with the PARC HBM FIP (parchbmfip) and the PARC TOXRIC FIP (parctoxric).",
