   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): The first formal description is Natale et al., 'Framework for a protein ontology', in the TMBIO '06 workshop proceedings (ACM), 2006-11-10. The journal version is BMC Bioinformatics 8(Suppl 9):S1, 2007-11-27. The PIR PRO page was captured on 2007-02-11 and cites 'Natale et al., 2006'. FAIRsharing.4ndncv (Standard/terminology_artefact, year 2006) was found through DataCite/Bioregistry and confirmed with one lookup. Current release is 73.0 (2026-07-01). I filled the creator, which was empty. Verified 5 Oct 2026: fairsharingMatch changed (One JSON lookup of https://fairsharing.org/FAIRsharing.4ndncv returns 'PRotein Ontology' (PRO), Standard/terminology_artefact, status ready, homepage https://proconsortium.org/. Name and homepage match.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Ontology used as a controlled vocabulary of protein forms with stable identifiers for precisely annotating proteins in pathways and key events.",
