   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. The previous inventory value 2014 (to verify) was the format paper: Ruusmann et al., J Cheminform, online 2014-05-14, doi 10.1186/1758-2946-6-25. The repository paper is Ruusmann et al. 2015 (doi 10.1186/s13321-015-0082-6, the one FAIRsharing cites). The first item in the repository was made available on 2012-05-14 (handle 10967/4), and the repository was archived live on 2013-03-31. The qsardb.org site with the format specification existed by 2009-02-27 (archive); FAIRsharing year is 2008. QsarDB stands for 'QSAR DataBank'; FAIRsharing's name 'QSAR DataBase' is inaccurate. The FAIRsharing record has a DOI, so its code FAIRsharing.ad3e10 replaces the numeric id 4904. Scope set to Life Sciences because the repository covers QSAR/QSPR for any endpoint; FAIRsharing subjects are broad, from chemistry to materials. Toxicology/In silico research would also be defensible. Verified 5 Oct 2026: fairsharingRecord changed (Minor consistency fix. The FAIRsharing record has DOI 10.25504/FAIRsharing.ad3e10 (in the fairsharing block, and @id already uses it). The row's research note says this code replaces the numeric id 4904, but the field was not updated.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Repository that accepts QSAR models and data with persistent handles, indexing them so in silico models can be found and reused.",
