   ],
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.9qv71f",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): I corrected the date from 2003. sbml.org says the SBML Level 1 Version 1 specification was 'made available on 2001-03-02'. The 2003 Bioinformatics paper (doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btg015, 2003-03-01) was the previous source and is a later description. FAIRsharing year 1999 is the project start; the SBML FAQ says the name was conceived around 2000. Initial development to 2003 was funded through the ERATO Kitano project at Caltech. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: An XML language for encoding computational models of biological processes so that machines can exchange, reuse and simulate them.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource"
