   "creator": "Karolinska Institutet; Stockholm University",
   "url": "https://www.scirap.org",
   "description": "A web resource from Karolinska Institutet and Stockholm University. It offers criteria and tools for evaluating the reliability and relevance of in vivo, in vitro, ecotoxicity (CRED) and epidemiological studies, plus reporting checklists for researchers. It makes study evaluations transparent and helps academic studies report what regulatory risk assessment needs.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "cited",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "V Challenges; L267",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): The earliest archive capture of scirap.org (2013-08-14) already shows evaluation criteria and reporting checklists, plus a news item on a 31 May thesis defence. So the site was online by mid-2013 (lower bound). Criteria proposed in Beronius et al., online 2014-01-30 (doi:10.1002/jat.2991); resource described in Molander et al., HERA, online 2014-09-30 (doi:10.1080/10807039.2014.928104). scirap.org now redirects to a Karolinska Institutet page updated in 2026. Added Stockholm University to creator, and eco-toxicology and in vitro toxicology to subdomains (SciRAP has CRED and in vitro tools). FAIRsharing: DataCite shows no FAIRsharing DOI; the web search budget was used up. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Web tool checking studies against reporting, reliability and relevance criteria, applied when researchers report studies and when assessors evaluate them.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Supporting-Resource",
   "qualifiedAttribution": [
