   "description": "A CDISC standard that specifies how data from nonclinical (animal) toxicology studies are organised, formatted and coded for exchange and electronic submission to regulators such as the US FDA. Its implementation guides define domains, variables and controlled terminology so study data can be reviewed, pooled and reused consistently.",
   "maintained": "active",
   "manuscript": "cited",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "III Regulatory; L178, L188, L193",
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.7z842d",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (medium confidence): Changed 2011 to 2004: cdisc.org hosted the public SEND Review Version 1.4 by 2004-05-19 (earliest Wayback capture, a lower bound). It was followed by v1.5 (2004), Implementation Guide v2.0 (by Jan 2005) and v2.3 (2006). SENDIG v3.0 (2011-06-17) is the earliest version CDISC lists today and matches the FAIRsharing year 2011; use it if only current versions count. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Exchange model and controlled terminology applied when nonclinical study datasets are produced, then used to pool studies and for FDA regulatory review.",
