   ],
   "dateReleased": "2006",
   "dateSource": "http://web.archive.org/web/20060320041511/http://www.leadscope.com/toxml.php",
   "creator": "Leadscope; Lhasa Limited",
   "url": "https://doi.org/10.1080/1062936X.2013.783506",
   "description": "An open XML schema with a controlled vocabulary for recording toxicity studies and endpoints (e.g. genetic toxicity, carcinogenicity, repeated-dose toxicity) in enough detail for database integration and (Q)SAR modelling. Leadscope developed it and Lhasa Limited later hosted it; it gave toxicity data from different sources a common exchange structure. Its website is no longer online.",
   "maintained": "discontinued",
   "manuscript": "absent",
   "mentionedIn": [
    "FAIRSharing"
   ],
   "fairsharingRecord": "FAIRsharing.emw61v",
   "fairsharingMatch": "confirmed",
   "note": "Added from the FAIRsharing Toxicology collection on 2026-10-05. Research 5 Oct 2026 (low confidence): FAIRsharing year 2011 replaced. Richard, Yang & Judson 2008 describe ToxML as an existing public standard, and Yang et al. 2008 use it (Toxicol Mech Methods 18(2-3)). Leadscope offered the public schema for download (archived page 2009-05-18). The dedicated paper, Ali et al. 2013 (Lhasa), is used as url. toxml.org no longer resolves (FAIRsharing status: deprecated). The origin, around 2005-2007, could not be dated more precisely. Verified 5 Oct 2026: datePublished changed (An earlier documented public release exists. The Wayback capture of Leadscope's ToxML page from 2006-03-20 (http://web.archive.org/web/20060320041511/http://www.leadscope.com/toxml.php) describes ToxML as an XML database standard based on a toxicity controlled vocabulary and offers 'Download the public ToxML schema (version 2.0)'. The page shows copyright 2005 and a LIST Consortium meeting of 5-7 Oct 2005. This lower bound predates Richard et al. 2008 (doi:10.1080/15376510701857452). Leadscope homepage captures from 2004-2005 do not mention ToxML, and the 2006 toxml.org capture is an unrelated German placeholder page, so 2006 is the earliest documented year.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateBasis changed (The earliest evidence is the public schema download on Leadscope's ToxML page, captured 2006-03-20 (http://web.archive.org/web/20060320041511/http://www.leadscope.com/toxml.php). That is a public release, not a describing paper.) Verified 5 Oct 2026: dateSource changed (This archived page shows 'Download the public ToxML schema (version 2.0)' by 2006-03-20, earlier than the 2008 paper. It is the earliest web-archive capture, so it is a lower bound.) Proposed 9 Oct 2026: An XML schema with controlled vocabulary that structures toxicity study results for exchange, database integration and QSAR modelling.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Enabling-Resource",
   "qualifiedAttribution": [
    {
     "@type": "prov:Attribution",
     "hadRole": "In silico research"
    }
   ]
  },
