   "creator": "EC JRC (ECVAM); FoBiG",
   "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.toxlet.2009.05.013",
   "description": "An Excel-based tool, made in an ECVAM-funded project, with criteria for judging the reliability of in vivo and in vitro toxicity studies and assigning them to Klimisch categories 1 to 3. It makes reliability judgements explicit and harmonised, which supports reuse of published and non-guideline studies in regulatory assessment.",
   "maintained": "unknown",
   "manuscript": "cited",
   "manuscriptEvidence": "IV (to-do notes); V Challenges; L212, L267",
   "note": "Research 5 Oct 2026 (high confidence): Schneider et al., Toxicol Lett 189(2):138-144; PubMed e-pub 2009-05-27 (accepted 2009-05-19). The ECVAM download page (archived 2013-2015) now redirects to the general EURL ECVAM page, and no current download was found, so maintained is 'unknown'. Included as guidance that supports data reuse, like CRED and SciRAP. It is borderline for I5 because it evaluates data rather than describing it. Added the in vitro toxicology subdomain (the tool has a separate in vitro part). FAIRsharing: DataCite shows no FAIRsharing DOI; the web search budget was used up. Proposed 9 Oct 2026: Tool that checks toxicity studies against reliability criteria and assigns Klimisch categories, applied when studies are evaluated for regulatory use.",
   "fsrCategory": "https://w3id.org/fair/fip/terms/FAIR-Supporting-Resource",
   "qualifiedAttribution": [
    {
     "@type": "prov:Attribution",
     "hadRole": "Regulator"
    }
   ]
  },
